{"seq":2,"slug":"fables-and-allegories","title":"Fables And Allegories","docCount":2,"url":"/c/people/zhuangzi/major-works/fables-and-allegories","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"teaching-through-stories","title":"以故事说理","url":"/c/people/zhuangzi/major-works/fables-and-allegories/teaching-through-stories","wordCount":1613,"readingTime":7},{"seq":2,"slug":"cook-ding-and-others","title":"庖丁解牛与濠梁观鱼","url":"/c/people/zhuangzi/major-works/fables-and-allegories/cook-ding-and-others","wordCount":1837,"readingTime":8}],"introMarkdown":"本章考察庄子\"以故事说理\"的独特表达方式。庄子通过\"三言\"（寓言、重言、卮言）——尤其是生动、奇特、深刻的寓言，将抽象的哲学思想化为形象的艺术，重在启发与领悟，创造了一种将哲学与文学完美结合的独特文体。本章还细读\"庖丁解牛\"（顺应自然的智慧）与\"濠梁观鱼\"（与万物相通的境界）等经典寓言，揭示其多重意蕴与永恒价值。\n"}